profile: runtime-mirust.next-recursive-prompt.v5
updated_utc: 2026-07-01T14:50:00Z
prompt: >
  Continue in E:\Source\Rust\SLMComposer.com as the active Rust workspace for SLMComposer.com / TinyRustLM. The site-folder split and source-control cleanup are complete: Runtime.MiRust.com is the plain-PHP documentation site, SLMComposer.com is the Rust/WASM app workspace, and MiniModel.org has a local ROADMAP.md. The seven MiniModel.org Improvement intake reports were authorized, copied byte-exact into docs/report-intake/2026-07-01/, synthesized, routed into wiki/runtime-mirust/research/minimodel-p2p-tiny-model-exchange-roadmap-2026-07-01.md, and removed from active intake. Start the next work from MiniModel.org roadmap implementation planning, keeping SLMComposer.com browser-local and keeping project servers metadata-only: no server-side user model execution and no project-server user model bytes.
primary_goal: >
  Turn the MiniModel.org roadmap into an implementable Rust-first plan for checksum-bound manifests, local verification/import receipts, metadata-only catalog entries, and a later peer-transfer app without changing SLMComposer.com's browser-local trust boundary.
required_context:
  - E:\Source\Rust\workspace.uai
  - workspace.uai
  - .uai/index.uai
  - .uai/file-handoff.uai
  - .uai/short-term-memory.uai
  - .uai/report-synthesis.uai
  - .uai/long-term-memory.uai
  - .uai/workspace-guidance.uai
  - docs/report-intake/2026-07-01/MANIFEST.md
  - docs/report-intake/2026-07-01/minimodel-p2p-report-synthesis-2026-07-01.md
  - wiki/runtime-mirust/research/minimodel-p2p-tiny-model-exchange-roadmap-2026-07-01.md
  - E:\Source\Rust\MiniModel.org\ROADMAP.md
processed_intake_routes:
  docs_manifest: docs/report-intake/2026-07-01/MANIFEST.md
  docs_synthesis: docs/report-intake/2026-07-01/minimodel-p2p-report-synthesis-2026-07-01.md
  durable_roadmap: wiki/runtime-mirust/research/minimodel-p2p-tiny-model-exchange-roadmap-2026-07-01.md
  minimodel_site_roadmap: E:\Source\Rust\MiniModel.org\ROADMAP.md
  source_site_result: processed source-site copies removed from agent-file-handoff/Improvement/ after byte-exact preservation and pointer updates.
roadmap_guardrails:
  - Rust-first P2P model exchange architecture; evaluate Pear/Bare/Hyper as tradeoffs, not core SLMComposer dependencies.
  - Legal/liability boundaries must keep MiniModel.org as metadata/catalog guidance until legal review; no claims that third-party models are safe, legal, or endorsed.
  - Secure manifests must be checksum-bound and route source identity, model cards, license, tokenizer/config, eval/admission evidence, chunk/Merkle data, and signatures.
  - Tiny-model creation/import stays tied to TinyRustLM local review, conversion, validation, runtime-smoke, eval, admission, and local import receipts.
  - Project servers never run user model bytes and never serve user model bytes.
success_criteria:
  - Active intake buckets remain empty or placeholder-only.
  - SLMComposer.com remains browser-local and user-selected local `.slm` import remains the model byte boundary.
  - MiniModel.org implementation work starts with schemas, verifier, local receipts, metadata-only catalog, and peer-transfer planning in that order.
  - Long-term memory remains pointer-based and checksum-bearing.
  - Before claiming completion, run relevant pointer audits and `git diff --check`.
